  data: {
    LLM: "In Lowball, do not stay in the hand after the first draw unless you are drawing to a 7ndlow or better (e.g., holding A-2-3).\n\nThe 'Second Draw' trap: Many players overndcommit to a hand that failed to improve on the first draw. Be willing to fold on the second betting round if you still haven't paired your low cards.\n\nBluffing the 'Stand Pat': Standing pat on the first draw even with a mediocre hand can force opponents to fold, as it signals you already have a completed, powerful low hand.",
    Player: "In Lowball, do not stay in the hand after the first draw unless you are drawing to a 7ndlow or better (e.g., holding A-2-3).\n\nThe 'Second Draw' trap: Many players overndcommit to a hand that failed to improve on the first draw. Be willing to fold on the second betting round if you still haven't paired your low cards.\n\nBluffing the 'Stand Pat': Standing pat on the first draw even with a mediocre hand can force opponents to fold, as it signals you already have a completed, powerful low hand.",
